.TH LLAPI_MIRROR_RESYNC_MANY 3 2026-10-21 "Lustre User API" "Lustre Library Functions"
.SH NAME
llapi_mirror_resync_many, llapi_mirror_resync_many_params \- resync mirrors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <lustre/lustreapi.h>
.PP
.BI "int llapi_mirror_resync_many(int " fd ", struct llapi_layout *" layout ,
.BI "                             struct llapi_resync_comp *" comp_array ,
.BI "                             int " comp_size ", uint64_t " start ,
.BI "                             uint64_t " end );
.PP
.BI "int llapi_mirror_resync_many_params(int " fd ,
.BI "                                    struct llapi_layout *" layout ,
.BI "                                    struct llapi_resync_comp *" comp_array ,
.BI "                                    int " comp_size ", uint64_t " start ,
.BI "                                    uint64_t " end ,
.BI "                                    unsigned long " stats_interval_sec ,
.BI "                                    uint64_t " bandwidth_bytes_sec );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions resync the stale components of the mirrored (FLR) file
open on
.IR fd ,
whose layout is
.IR layout .
.I comp_array
holds the
.I comp_size
components to resync, as collected by
.BR llapi_mirror_find_stale_flags (3)
with
.BR LCME_FL_PARITY .
The caller must hold a resync lease on
.I fd
.RB ( LL_LEASE_RESYNC ),
and the file should be open with
.BR O_DIRECT ,
as
.BR lfs-mirror-resync (1)
does.
Read
.I layout
with
.BR llapi_layout_get_by_fd (3)
after taking the lease, as the lease instantiates the stale components.
.PP
The data components are copied from an in-sync mirror over the file range
.RI [ start ", " end ).
Holes in the source are punched in the stale components, and a component
that extends to the end of the file is truncated there, unless it is not
instantiated.
Then the parity
.RB ( LCME_FL_PARITY )
components of an Erasure Coded (EC) file are recomputed whole from the data
components they protect. A parity component whose data component is in
.I comp_array
and was not synced is not synced either, nor is one whose data component is
stale and not in
.IR comp_array .
A parity component with no data component, as left by a mirror split, or
with an EC layout version this library does not know, cannot be recomputed:
it is skipped with a warning, without an error, and stays stale, with
.I lrc_synced
cleared.
.PP
.BR llapi_mirror_resync_many_params ()
also takes
.IR stats_interval_sec ,
the interval in seconds between progress lines printed to standard output,
or 0 for none, and
.IR bandwidth_bytes_sec ,
the bandwidth to limit the resync to, in bytes per second, or 0 for no
limit. Both count the data copied and the parity written in one total.
.BR llapi_mirror_resync_many ()
does the same with neither.
.PP
On return, the
.I lrc_synced
field of each entry of
.I comp_array
tells whether that component was synced. An error in one component does not
undo the others, so the caller can still clear
.B LCME_FL_STALE
of the components that were synced, by releasing the lease with
.B LL_LEASE_RESYNC_DONE
and their component ids.
.SH RETURN VALUES
Both functions return 0 if every component was synced, or skipped as a
parity component with no data component or an unknown EC layout version,
or else the first negative errno encountered.
Check
.I lrc_synced
of each entry to tell which components were synced.
.SH ERRORS
.TP 15
.B -ENOENT
No in-sync mirror covers part of the range to copy.
.TP 15
.B -ENOMEM
Insufficient memory to complete the operation.
.TP 15
.B -EINVAL
A parity component does not match its data component in extent or stripe
size, or its data component is stale and not in
.IR comp_array .
.PP
Errors from reading, writing, punching or truncating the mirrors, for
example
.BR -EIO ,
are also returned.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.BR llapi_mirror_find_stale (3).
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B llapi_mirror_resync_many()
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
user application interface library since release 2.12.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_11_53_0-45-g0e5c12ac29a9
.B llapi_mirror_resync_many_params()
is part of it since release 2.16.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_15_57-36-gbe131d125ad1
Parity components are resynced by these functions since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_62-xxx-gxxxxxxxxxxx
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfs-mirror-resync (1),
.BR llapi_lease_set (3),
.BR llapi_mirror_find_stale (3),
.BR llapi_layout (7),
.BR lustreapi (7)
